WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.867 --> 00:00:21.226
The next winter, the aches in Jehan's bones made it too difficult for him to move.

2
00:00:21.227 --> 00:00:24.352
He had been crippled for years.

3
00:00:24.353 --> 00:00:30.664
But now, it was impossible for him even to walk beside the cart.

4
00:00:30.665 --> 00:00:34.423
Little Nello was now six years old.

5
00:00:34.424 --> 00:00:41.248
He knew Antwerp well because he had accompanied his grandfather there many times.

6
00:00:41.249 --> 00:00:48.903
So, Nello took Jehan's place beside the cart and walked with Patrasche instead.

7
00:00:48.904 --> 00:00:54.641
Nello sold the milk in Antwerp and received the coins in exchange.

8
00:00:54.642 --> 00:00:59.015
He brought the money back to the farmers in the village.

9
00:00:59.016 --> 00:01:02.358
He did all his work with an innocent dignity;

10
00:01:02.359 --> 00:01:07.887
everyone who met him was charmed.

11
00:01:07.888 --> 00:01:15.957
Nello was a beautiful child, with tender eyes, a lovely face, and light blond hair.

12
00:01:15.958 --> 00:01:23.294
Often when Nello and Patrasche were walking into town, an artist stopped them on the road.

13
00:01:23.295 --> 00:01:27.792
He would ask little Nello if he could sketch him.

14
00:01:27.793 --> 00:01:34.867
Since Nello and Patrasche were never in a rush, Nello usually agreed.

15
00:01:34.868 --> 00:01:39.697
Besides, Nello loved seeing the finished sketch.

16
00:01:39.698 --> 00:01:48.584
The artist would carefully draw Nello and Patrasche with the fields of Flanders in the background.

17
00:01:48.585 --> 00:01:55.323
Nello and Patrasche delivered the milk so well that Jehan did not worry.

18
00:01:55.324 --> 00:02:00.533
On summer mornings, he sat in the sunlit doorway of the hut.

19
00:02:00.534 --> 00:02:04.639
He watched the happy pair head down the road.

20
00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:10.603
In the afternoon, he rested and then watched for their return.

21
00:02:10.604 --> 00:02:17.281
At the hut, Patrasche would shake himself free of his harness with a happy bark.

22
00:02:17.282 --> 00:02:22.888
Nello would proudly tell his grandfather everything they had done.

23
00:02:22.889 --> 00:02:27.933
Then they would all eat a dinner of rye bread and soup.

24
00:02:27.934 --> 00:02:33.606
At the end of each day, the shadows grew long in the pastures.

25
00:02:33.607 --> 00:02:38.931
The distant spire of the great cathedral faded in the twilight.

26
00:02:38.932 --> 00:02:46.561
At night, Nello and Patrasche lay down together while the old man said a prayer.

27
00:02:46.562 --> 00:02:50.101
So the days and the years went on.

28
00:02:50.102 --> 00:02:55.062
The lives of Nello and Patrasche were happy and innocent.

29
00:02:55.063 --> 00:03:01.926
Flanders is not a place of majestic beauty, but the land is green and wide.

30
00:03:01.927 --> 00:03:06.915
Its spacious horizons are pleasant and welcoming.

31
00:03:06.916 --> 00:03:15.261
In summer, fall, and spring, little Nello and Patrasche would lie in the grass beside the canal.

32
00:03:15.262 --> 00:03:22.302
They watched the boats drift by and breathed the salty air of the sea.

33
00:03:22.303 --> 00:03:25.720
In the winter, life was harder.

34
00:03:25.721 --> 00:03:30.042
They had to get up in the dark and the bitter cold.

35
00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:37.237
The hut was not much warmer than a shed, and the wind found many holes in the walls.

36
00:03:37.238 --> 00:03:42.441
The bare fields around the hut looked flat and grim.

37
00:03:42.442 --> 00:03:47.172
The cold pinched little Nello's hands and toes.

38
00:03:47.173 --> 00:03:52.898
The snow and ice cut the brave, tireless feet of Patrasche.

39
00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:56.375
But the two friends never complained.

40
00:03:56.376 --> 00:04:05.222
They walked over the frozen fields together, accompanied by the chime of the bells on Patrasche's harness.

41
00:04:05.223 --> 00:04:13.674
Sometimes, in the streets of Antwerp, a housewife would bring them a bowl of soup and a handful of bread.

42
00:04:13.675 --> 00:04:23.083
Sometimes, a kindly merchant would throw a little firewood into the small cart as they went home.

43
00:04:23.084 --> 00:04:28.318
Patrasche worked through the heat of summer and the chills of winter.

44
00:04:28.319 --> 00:04:34.109
Even though he was often hungry, he was grateful and content.

45
00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:39.798
As Patrasche worked, the eyes that he loved smiled down on him.

46
00:04:39.799 --> 00:04:46.365
It was enough.
